//==
// # The closed-form grid counts of an analytic face: types (TKT-502, chunk QF1)
//
// Layer 05-face-meshing. A structured grid on a cylinder, cone, sphere or torus face can be sized
// in closed form: an arc of radius R and sweep theta whose chords may deviate by d needs
// ceil(theta / (2 acos(1 - d / R))) segments, layer 04's ArcCriteriaCount, which already sizes the
// model's circles. These types say what the formula sees of a face: a direction and a chordal
// budget per parameter.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Directions
//  - Formulas
//  - Counts
//  - Witness cases

//==
// # Directions

// One parameter direction of a grid on an analytic surface, as the chordal formula sees it.
//   Circular: a circle of the given radius, the largest parallel the face reaches in that
//     direction (a cone's widest parallel, a sphere's parallel nearest the equator), to be cut
//     into segments whose chords meet the budget.
//   Straight: a ruling (a cylinder's or cone's axis direction), which one cell spans exactly.
//   Unknown: the formula says nothing (a B-spline, a surface of revolution, an offset).
type GridDirection
    = Circular(Radius: Number)
    | Straight
    | Unknown;

//==
// # Formulas

// What the formula says about a face's grid over the region's parameter box. Budget is the chordal
// deviation each circular direction may spend: the face's whole SurfaceChordal on a face curved one
// way (a cylinder, a cone), half of it on a face curved both ways (a sphere, a torus), whose cell
// deviates by about the sum of its two sagittas.
type GridFormula
{
    U: GridDirection;
    V: GridDirection;
    Budget: Number;
}

//==
// # Counts

// The segment counts the formula asks of a region's two directions: 0 where it asks nothing (an
// Unknown direction), 1 for a straight one, the arc count for a circular one.
type FormulaCounts
    implements IValue
{
    U: Integer;
    V: Integer;
}

//==
// # Witness cases

// One arc for the laws of the count: a circle of Radius, a sweep in radians, and the chordal budget
// its chords may spend.
type ArcCase
{
    Radius: Number;
    Sweep: Number;
    Budget: Number;
}
